= OCPPProxy User Manual =

The '''OCPPProxy''' is an [https://www.openchargealliance.org/ OCPP 1.6] WebSocket proxy (man‑in‑the‑middle) that sits between EV charge points and one or more central systems (CSMS). It transparently forwards OCPP messages in both directions while logging, inspecting, optionally modifying, and selectively blocking them. A real‑time web dashboard provides monitoring and control.

This manual describes how to '''install''', '''configure''', and '''use''' the OCPPProxy.

__TOC__

== Overview ==

The OCPPProxy provides:

* '''Bidirectional message proxying''' between charge points and up to '''3 backend CSMS''' servers (fan‑out forwarding).
* '''Real‑time logging''' of all OCPP messages with request/response pairing.
* '''Command blocking''' — reject specific OCPP commands globally or per charge point.
* '''BootNotification overrides''' — rewrite vendor/model/serial/firmware/meter fields per charge point.
* '''Connector control''' — inject <code>ChangeAvailability</code> commands and override reported connector status.
* '''Web dashboard''' with live Socket.IO updates, statistics, and an equipment database.
* '''Automatic backend reconnection''' with message buffering during outages.
* '''SQLite persistence''' for configuration, message history, and statistics.

=== Architecture ===

<pre>
Charge Points
     │  (OCPP / WebSocket)  ws://<proxy>:9100/ocpp/<cp_id>
     ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│            OCPPProxy               │
│  Port 9100 — charge point listener │
│  Port 4000 — web dashboard         │
└────────────────────────────────────┘
     │  fan-out to up to 3 backends
     ▼
Central System(s) (CSMS)   ws://<backend>:9000/ocpp/<cp_id>
</pre>

{| class="wikitable"
! Component !! File !! Responsibility
|-
| Entry point || <code>ocppproxy.py</code> || Starts the web dashboard and the background WebSocket proxy thread; configures logging
|-
| Proxy engine || <code>proxy_core.py</code> || WebSocket server, message forwarding, blocking, overrides, reconnection
|-
| Web GUI + API || <code>web_app.py</code> || Flask + Socket.IO dashboard and REST API
|-
| Database layer || <code>proxy_db.py</code> || SQLite schema and data access
|}

== Installation ==

=== Requirements ===

* '''Python 3''' (uses <code>asyncio</code>, <code>eventlet</code>, and f‑strings).
* Packages from <code>requirements.txt</code>:

{| class="wikitable"
! Package !! Purpose
|-
| <code>flask>=3.0</code> || Web dashboard and REST API
|-
| <code>flask-socketio>=5.4</code> || Real‑time dashboard updates
|-
| <code>python-engineio>=4.9</code>, <code>python-socketio>=5.11</code> || Socket.IO transport
|-
| <code>eventlet</code> || Async worker / monkey‑patching for gunicorn
|-
| <code>websockets</code> || OCPP WebSocket client/server
|}

=== Install steps ===

# Create the application, data, and log directories:
#: <pre>sudo mkdir -p /opt/charger/OCPPProxy /opt/charger/data /var/log/charger</pre>
# Copy the OCPPProxy source files into <code>/opt/charger/OCPPProxy/</code>.
# Create a virtual environment and install dependencies:
#: <pre>cd /opt/charger/OCPPProxy
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt</pre>

=== Running manually (development) ===

<pre>
python3 ocppproxy.py
</pre>

This starts the web dashboard on port '''4000''' and the OCPP proxy listener on port '''9100'''. The database is initialised automatically on first run.

=== Running in production (gunicorn) ===

The entry module exposes the Flask <code>app</code> object and is run under gunicorn with the eventlet worker. The proxy thread starts automatically when the module loads:

<pre>
gunicorn --worker-class eventlet --workers 1 --bind 0.0.0.0:4000 app:app
</pre>

{{Note|Use a single worker (<code>--workers 1</code>). The OCPP proxy runs in a background thread inside the worker; multiple workers would start multiple conflicting listeners.}}

=== Running as a systemd service ===

A service unit is provided (<code>systemd/charger-ocppproxy.service</code>):

<pre>
[Unit]
Description=OCPP Proxy Server
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=notify
WorkingDirectory=/opt/charger/OCPPProxy
Environment="PATH=/opt/charger/OCPPProxy/venv/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin"
Environment="OCPP_UPSTREAM_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:9000/ocpp"
Environment="PROXY_LISTEN_PORT=9100"
Environment="PROXY_DATA_DIR=/opt/charger/data"
Environment="PROXY_LOG_DIR=/var/log/charger"
ExecStart=/opt/charger/OCPPProxy/venv/bin/gunicorn \
    --worker-class eventlet \
    --workers 1 \
    --bind 0.0.0.0:4000 \
    --timeout 120 \
    --access-logfile /var/log/charger/OCPPProxy.access.log \
    --error-logfile /var/log/charger/OCPPProxy.error.log \
    --log-level info \
    app:app
StandardOutput=append:/var/log/charger/OCPPProxy.stdout
StandardError=append:/var/log/charger/OCPPProxy.stderr
Restart=always
RestartSec=10
KillMode=mixed
KillSignal=SIGTERM
User=karl
Group=lovink

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
</pre>

To install and enable the service:

<pre>
sudo cp systemd/charger-ocppproxy.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now charger-ocppproxy
</pre>

{{Note|The gunicorn target <code>app:app</code> expects the entry module to be importable as <code>app</code>. Deploy the entry file as <code>app.py</code> in the working directory (or adjust the target to match the module name).}}

